<title>GERMANY: Bayer sees 1997 group sales over 50 bln dmk.</title>
<headline>Bayer sees 1997 group sales over 50 bln dmk.</headline>
<dateline>LEVERKUSEN, Germany 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemical group Bayer AG said on Wednesday that it expected group sales in 1997 to total over 50 billion marks ($29 billion).</p>
<p>For 1996, the company reported sales of 48.6 billion marks.</p>
<p>The forecast was made at the company's annual shareholder meeting.</p>
<p>Bayer said first-quarter parent company pre-tax profit dipped to 650 million marks from 680 million, on sales up at 4.852 billion marks from 4.685 billion.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
